# Negamane Cross-Platform Model

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    N[Negamane Integrity Boundary] --> L[Linux / Ubuntu White]
    N --> W[Windows-derived implementation]
    L --> E[EXT4 / Linux storage evidence]
    W --> NT[NTFS or ReFS / Windows storage evidence]
    N --> S[Shared logical schema]
    S --> G[18 generic ratings]
    S --> H[Per-copy overall health]
    S --> A[Alteration history]
    S --> C[Three-copy relationship]
    N --> B[Base Filesystem Mode]
    B --> O[One ordinary file copy]
```

Base Filesystem Mode is an explicit space-saving installation choice. It is not represented as a three-copy configuration.
